Modifications
-------------
Copyright 2026 Wael Mansour.
Source: https://github.com/wamansou/ninfer-tp2-1m
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

This tree is a fork of Neroued/ninfer at commit feaf4dd. The modifications add
tensor-parallel execution across two GPUs and YaRN positional scaling for
1,048,576-token contexts to the 27B execution package. They touch, in summary:

  * src/core           two-device ExecutionContext; per-device arenas, streams
                       and graph objects; per-device memoization of kernel
                       attribute opt-ins
  * src/ops            allreduce_sum and allgather collectives; column- and
                       row-parallel split forms of the nine Op families that
                       carry sharded weights; a 12-Q-head/2-KV-head GQA
                       geometry; a YaRN frequency-buffer rope kernel; a
                       1,048,576-key visible-key domain and the shared-memory
                       accounting that goes with it
  * src/artifact       sharded weight and shard plans, and the materialization
                       that binds a shard of a tensor to one device
  * src/targets        two-rank Program wiring: split prefill, decode, MTP and
                       output-head schedules; cross-device graph capture and
                       replay; peer state publication
  * src/runtime,       --tp / --devices / --rope / --yarn-* plumbing through the
    src/serve, apps    public Engine, the CLI and the server
  * eval/, tools/tp2/  1M needle, soak and power runners; P2P, capture and
                       transport probes; the tp1-to-tp2 parity harness; the
                       vLLM YaRN reference dumper
  * tests/, scripts/   split-Op oracles, dual-device integration and graph
                       tests, the YaRN drift guard, and the tp1 golden-token
                       identity gate against upstream feaf4dd

Single-GPU (--tp 1) behaviour is unchanged from feaf4dd; see
tests/data/tp1-golden/MANIFEST.md for the token-level comparison.

Modifications (Windows-TP2 layer)
--------------------------------
Copyright 2026 Dmitriy Ivanov.
Source: https://github.com/ivanov84/ninfer-windows-tp2
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

This tree is a fork of wamansou/ninfer-tp2-1m at commit 6a355d5 (branch windows-tp2).
The modifications add, in summary:

  * a native Windows 11 build of the TP2 engine (MSVC/vcpkg toolchain;
    CreateFileW/MapViewOfFile artifact reader; winsock media acquisition;
    MSVC-safe TMA descriptors and plan moves)
  * a pinned-host-memory peer mailbox transport (ops::PeerMailbox,
    peer_exchange_sum_kernel) for the small captured TP2 collectives, with the
    staged event-ordered path retained as the automatic fallback
  * vision support at --tp 2: the vision tower bound and materialized per rank
    (dual-replicated, 282 MiB per GPU), per-rank vision encode feeding the text
    TP2 prefill, a per-item pixel budget (2048 merged tokens / 2,097,152 px)
    with automatic smart_resize downscale, the MTP+vision rope-position fix in
    the tp2 draft stage, and per-request prefill-failure lane recovery
  * a second registered Qwen3.8-27B NVFP4 artifact identity (nvfp4-split) with
    TP2 column-shard siblings of the BF16 fused attention input projection
    kernels, so the split-storage Ostfralla export loads on two GPUs
  * MTP-related cleanup, build fixes, and the tp2 diagnostic set
    (mailbox_probe, reduce_bench, graph_launch_probe, profile analysis scripts)
  * documentation and benchmark records of the Windows-TP2 results

Portions of the Windows compatibility layer are derived from
natpate/ninfer-windows (https://github.com/natpate/ninfer-windows),
Copyright the natpate/ninfer-windows contributors, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE). Cherry-picked source commits:
8e7f596 (CMake/vcpkg Windows build), 965c67f (artifact reader, load
progress, console log), 0785bd3 (media acquire, request-log test),
9bc46ce (platform library routing), 48035f7+d7cc655+b408783 (TMA
descriptors, plan moves). The per-file mapping is documented in
docs/PROVENANCE.md.

Model artifacts
---------------
The published artifacts are derived from Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B, Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B and
Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, and from the packed-weight repackagings named in the
README's License section; the additional split-storage Qwen3.8-27B NVFP4 export
tested by this fork (published by Ostfralla) is a repackaging of the same
Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B checkpoint. Those source repositories are distributed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

Vendored dependencies retain their own license files under third_party/.
